.TH OROC-UPDATE-INFO 1 "" "Oro Runtime 0.1.1" "Oro Runtime Manual"
.SH NAME
oroc\-update\-info \- Query update servers or static manifests over HTTP/TCP/UDP.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
oroc update info [\-\-transport=<http|tcp|udp>] [options]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Query update servers or static manifests over HTTP/TCP/UDP.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-config=<path>\fR
use an explicit oro.toml/oro.ini file for local CHECK request defaults
.TP
\fB\-\-transport=<http|tcp|udp>\fR
transport to use (default: http)
.TP
\fB\-\-http\fR
shorthand for \-\-transport=http
.TP
\fB\-\-tcp\fR
shorthand for \-\-transport=tcp
.TP
\fB\-\-udp\fR
shorthand for \-\-transport=udp
.TP
\fB\-\-follow\-manifest\fR
when contacting servers, follow 'manifestUrl' in the RESPONSE and fetch/validate that manifest over HTTP(S)
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\-ms=<ms>\fR
optional timeout for TCP/UDP CHECK requests (0 = no timeout)
.TP
\fB\-\-manifest\-url=<url>\fR
HTTP(S) URL of a manifest.json hosted statically
.TP
\fB\-\-signature\-url=<url>\fR
optional HTTP(S) URL of the corresponding signature JSON (default: derived from \-\-manifest\-url)
.TP
\fB\-\-keys=<file>\fR
JSON file containing a public key ("publicKey" or "key" field) for manifest verification
.TP
\fB\-\-public\-key=<hex>\fR
Ed25519 public key as a hex string for manifest verification
.TP
\fB\-\-host=<host>\fR
host for HTTP/TCP/UDP update servers (default: 127.0.0.1)
.TP
\fB\-\-port=<port>\fR
port for HTTP/TCP/UDP update servers (default: 8080)
.TP
\fB\-\-app\-id=<id>\fR
application identifier to send in CHECK messages (default: active config meta.bundle_identifier when available)
.TP
\fB\-\-channel=<name>\fR
update channel hint (default: active config update_channel or "stable")
.TP
\fB\-\-current\-version=<version>\fR
current application version hint (default: active config meta.version when available)
.TP
\fB\-\-runtime\-version=<version>\fR
runtime version hint advertised in CHECK (optional)
.TP
\fB\-\-platform=<id>\fR
platform hint advertised in CHECK (optional)
.TP
\fB\-\-arch=<id>\fR
architecture hint advertised in CHECK (optional)
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-file=<path>\fR
mirror logs to a JSON file
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
With '\-\-manifest\-url', this command fetches and pretty\-prints a manifest JSON and reports whether a signature file is reachable.
.PP
When '\-\-keys' or '\-\-public\-key' is provided and libsodium is available, it also verifies the manifest signature before printing.
.IP \(bu 2
With HTTP/TCP/UDP transports and no '\-\-manifest\-url', it sends a CHECK message to an update server and pretty\-prints the RESPONSE JSON.
.PP
With '\-\-follow\-manifest', if the RESPONSE includes a 'manifestUrl', it will fetch, validate, and optionally verify that manifest as well. When '\-\-app\-id' is provided, the fetched manifest must have a matching 'appId' or the command exits with an error.
.IP \(bu 2
When building a CHECK request and '\-\-config' is omitted, this command looks for `oro.toml` first and falls back to
.PP
`oro.ini` in the current workspace to derive app\-id, channel, and current\-version defaults. Outside a project workspace, pass those values explicitly.
.IP \(bu 2
When using TCP/UDP, '\-\-timeout\-ms' can be used to bound how long the client waits for a response.
.IP \(bu 2
The flags '\-\-http', '\-\-tcp', and '\-\-udp' are shorthands for '\-\-transport=http', '\-\-transport=tcp', and '\-\-transport=udp' respectively.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBoroc update info \-\-manifest\-url https://cdn.example.com/app/manifest.json\fR
inspect a statically hosted manifest
.TP
\fBoroc update info \-\-manifest\-url https://cdn.example.com/app/manifest.json \-\-keys app\-pubkey.json\fR
fetch and verify a statically hosted manifest + signature
.TP
\fBoroc update info \-\-http \-\-host 127.0.0.1 \-\-port 8080 \-\-app\-id com.example.app \-\-follow\-manifest\fR
query an HTTP update server and then fetch the referenced manifest
.TP
\fBoroc update info \-\-tcp \-\-host 127.0.0.1 \-\-port 9000 \-\-app\-id com.example.app \-\-follow\-manifest\fR
query a TCP update server using the binary OUP protocol
.SH SEE ALSO
oroc(1), oroc\-update(1)
